---
import Legal from '@/layouts/Legal.astro';
import { LEGAL } from '@/config/site';
---

<Legal title="Privacy policy" description="How the Godmode website handles your data: cookieless analytics, optional X pixel, Stripe payments.">
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal data we process when you visit this website or buy Godmode, why, and what rights
    you have. The Godmode apps themselves, on your computer and on your phone, run on your devices, have no telemetry and
    send nothing to us; section 10 explains the phone app.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    {LEGAL.company}, {LEGAL.street}, {LEGAL.city}, {LEGAL.country} · <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.email}`}>{LEGAL.email}</a>
  </p>

  <h2>2. Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    The website is served by Cloudflare, Inc. (101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA) on our behalf. To deliver
    the pages and protect them against attacks, Cloudflare processes technical connection data such as your IP address,
    browser and time of access. Legal basis: Art. 6 (1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in a secure, working website).
    Cloudflare is certified under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework; we have a data processing agreement with Cloudflare.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Cookieless visitor statistics</h2>
  <p>
    We count visits and clicks on this site (for example “pricing viewed” or “checkout started”) with our own, cookieless
    analytics. We store the page, the event, the referring website’s domain, campaign parameters (utm_*), your country
    (derived by Cloudflare), a device class and a pseudonymous visitor ID. That ID is a keyed one-way hash (with a secret
    key) of the date, your IP address and your browser’s user-agent; it changes every day, and your IP address itself is
    never stored. The statistics set no cookies and store nothing on your device. Legal basis: Art. 6 (1)(f) GDPR
    (legitimate interest in understanding which parts of the site and which campaigns work). Events are deleted after 14
    months. We do keep your cookie choice in your browser’s local storage, and after a purchase a strictly necessary,
    signed session cookie (30 days) lets you reach your license, downloads and billing portal.
  </p>

  <h2>4. X (Twitter) pixel — only with your consent</h2>
  <p>
    If you click “Accept” in the cookie notice, we load the X conversion pixel from X Corp. (1355 Market Street, San
    Francisco, CA 94103, USA; for EU users, Twitter International Unlimited Company, Dublin). It sets cookies and sends
    X information about your visit and actions on this site (for example a purchase and its value), so we can measure
    which ads work and show ads to people who visited. X may link this to your X account. Legal basis: your consent,
    Art. 6 (1)(a) GDPR and § 25 (1) TDDDG. You can withdraw consent at any time via “Cookie settings” in the footer.
    With consent we also remember in your browser’s local storage which campaign brought you here, so a later purchase
    can be attributed to it.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Buying Godmode (Stripe)</h2>
  <p>
    Payments are processed by Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd. (1 Grand Canal Street Lower, Dublin, Ireland). When you
    check out, Stripe processes your name, email, billing address, payment details and, if you provide it, your VAT ID;
    we receive your name, email, country, the plan and amount, and never your full card details. We use this to fulfil
    the contract, issue invoices, provide support and meet tax and accounting obligations (Art. 6 (1)(b) and (c) GDPR).
    We link the purchase to the campaign that brought you here (Art. 6 (1)(f) GDPR). Invoicing records are kept for the
    statutory retention period (up to 10 years).
  </p>
  <p>
    Downloads and app updates are served through this website from our software repository; we log which build was
    requested, not who you are.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Playbook and launch emails</h2>
  <p>
    If you enter your email to get the playbook, we store it with the date and campaign source and email you about
    Godmode (Art. 6 (1)(a) GDPR). You can unsubscribe with the link in every email or by writing to us; we then delete
    your address.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Email contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we process your message to answer it (Art. 6 (1)(b) or (f) GDPR) and delete it when it’s no longer
    needed, unless retention obligations apply.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Transfers outside the EU</h2>
  <p>
    Cloudflare, X and Stripe may process data in the USA. Transfers rely on the EU–US Data Privacy Framework and/or the
    EU Standard Contractual Clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability and to object to
    processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 15–21 GDPR), and to withdraw consent at any time with effect for the
    future. You can also lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority, for example the Landesbeauftragte für den
    Datenschutz und die Informationsfreiheit Baden-Württemberg. Just email <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.email}`}>{LEGAL.email}</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>10. The Godmode phone app (iOS and Android)</h2>
  <p>
    The Godmode app for iPhone, iPad and Android is a remote control for Godmode on your own computer. It connects only to
    that computer, over your private Tailscale network, and sends nothing to us: no account, no analytics, no crash
    reports, no ads. We don’t collect personal data through the app. The camera is used only to scan the pairing QR code
    and no images leave the phone. On Android, the QR scanner is Google’s ML Kit (part of Google Play services), which
    sends Google technical usage data about the scanner, such as device and app information, performance metrics and
    error codes; see Google’s ML Kit data disclosure. The key your phone receives when pairing is kept in the phone’s secure storage (the
    Keychain on iOS, Keystore-protected storage on Android). Chats, agents and screens are loaded from your computer while
    you use the app. Tailscale Inc. provides the network connection under its own terms and privacy policy. You can
    remove a phone at any time in Godmode on your computer under Settings → Phone.
  </p>
</Legal>
